---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About">
  <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-4 text-brand-light">About</h1>

  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 text-brand">Why this project?</h2>
    <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mb-4">
      This homelab started as a single Raspberry Pi 4B running Docker containers for personal services.
      It grew into a two-node mesh with a full observability + secrets + auth stack on a second machine —
      then that entire stack got retired once it was clear it wasn't earning its RAM. What's left is a lean
      core that actually gets used daily, with every major decision (and reversal) documented as it happened.
    </p>
    <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
      The project demonstrates infrastructure-as-code practices applied to a homelab:
      Docker Compose orchestration, mesh VPN networking, DNS filtering, security hardening,
      and the discipline to cut back down once the actual usage pattern was clear — all on a $35 board.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6 text-brand">Tech Stack</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <div class="border border-surface-light rounded-lg p-4 bg-surface-light/20">
        <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">Infrastructure</h3>
        <ul class="text-sm text-text-muted space-y-1">
          <li>Raspberry Pi 4B (4GB) + 1.9TB SSD</li>
          <li>Debian Trixie (aarch64)</li>
          <li>Docker Compose (no Kubernetes)</li>
          <li>Tailscale mesh VPN</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-surface-light rounded-lg p-4 bg-surface-light/20">
        <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">Networking</h3>
        <ul class="text-sm text-text-muted space-y-1">
          <li>Headscale (self-hosted mesh control plane)</li>
          <li>Pi-hole DNS ad-blocking</li>
          <li>Samba + Syncthing (file access &amp; sync)</li>
          <li>Direct mesh-IP:port per service — no reverse proxy layer</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-surface-light rounded-lg p-4 bg-surface-light/20">
        <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">Observability</h3>
        <ul class="text-sm text-text-muted space-y-1">
          <li>Uptime Kuma (up/down + response time)</li>
          <li>Netdata (real-time system + container metrics)</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-xs text-text-muted mt-2">
          Prometheus/Grafana/Loki/Tempo/Alertmanager were built, ran, then retired
          (ADR-009) — full stack was disproportionate for a single-operator setup.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-surface-light rounded-lg p-4 bg-surface-light/20">
        <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">Security</h3>
        <ul class="text-sm text-text-muted space-y-1">
          <li>Vaultwarden (passwords)</li>
          <li>Headscale mesh membership as the access boundary</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-xs text-text-muted mt-2">
          Authelia/Infisical/CrowdSec were built, then retired — no multi-user
          need, no rotation workflow ever actually used (ADR-009).
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 text-brand">Timeline</h2>
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="flex gap-4">
        <div class="shrink-0 w-24 text-sm text-text-muted text-right">v1.0</div>
        <div class="border-l-2 border-brand pl-4">
          <p class="font-medium">Initial setup</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">Docker Compose on Pi 4B with basic stacks</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-4">
        <div class="shrink-0 w-24 text-sm text-text-muted text-right">v1.1</div>
        <div class="border-l-2 border-brand pl-4">
          <p class="font-medium">K3s experiment</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">Kubernetes with ArgoCD, Helmfile - too heavy for 4GB Pi</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-4">
        <div class="shrink-0 w-24 text-sm text-text-muted text-right">v1.2</div>
        <div class="border-l-2 border-brand pl-4">
          <p class="font-medium">K3s removed, optimized</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">Docker Compose only, swap off, TinyBot, Tailscale mesh</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-4">
        <div class="shrink-0 w-24 text-sm text-text-muted text-right">v1.3</div>
        <div class="border-l-2 border-brand pl-4">
          <p class="font-medium">Multi-node mesh</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">Pi always-on core + Windows heavy compute, restructured repo</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-4">
        <div class="shrink-0 w-24 text-sm text-text-muted text-right">v1.4</div>
        <div class="border-l-2 border-brand pl-4">
          <p class="font-medium">Container hardening</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">Pinned tags, healthchecks, CPU limits, :ro mounts, stale cleanup</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-4">
        <div class="shrink-0 w-24 text-sm text-text-muted text-right">v1.5</div>
        <div class="border-l-2 border-brand pl-4">
          <p class="font-medium">Security audit</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">STRIDE review, Redis auth, TinyBot hardening, network hardening</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-4">
        <div class="shrink-0 w-24 text-sm text-text-muted text-right">v1.6&ndash;v1.8</div>
        <div class="border-l-2 border-brand pl-4">
          <p class="font-medium">Headscale, Gitea, Hub dashboard</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">Self-hosted mesh control plane replaces Tailscale SaaS; self-hosted git + CI/CD; unified service launcher</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-4">
        <div class="shrink-0 w-24 text-sm text-text-muted text-right">v2</div>
        <div class="border-l-2 border-brand pl-4">
          <p class="font-medium">Identity + repo consolidation</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">Three drifting repo copies merged into one canonical source, migrated into indexed Samba storage</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-4">
        <div class="shrink-0 w-24 text-sm text-text-muted text-right">v2.1</div>
        <div class="border-l-2 border-brand-light pl-4">
          <p class="font-medium text-brand-light">The retirement (current)</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">
            Windows observability/secrets/auth stack (11 containers), Traefik, Portainer, CrowdSec,
            Home Assistant retired per ADR-009 — moved to <code>_retired/</code>, then removed from the
            working tree entirely (recoverable via git history, nothing deleted). Netdata replaces the
            six-container metrics stack it made obsolete. Down to 8 services that actually get used.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 text-brand">Links</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-2 text-text-muted">
      <li><a href="http://100.64.0.1:8087/vansh/pi-utility-server" class="text-brand-light hover:underline">Gitea Repository</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/iamvanshkhanna" class="text-brand-light hover:underline">GitHub</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://linkedin.com/in/iamvanshkhanna" class="text-brand-light hover:underline">LinkedIn</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>
